138
00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:44.860
water.
水。

139
00:06:45.260 --> 00:06:51.440
You dirty all their towels and walk out naked where they're having a children's party in
你弄脏了他们所有的毛巾，然后光着身子走出去，而他们当时正在屋里

140
00:06:51.440 --> 00:06:51.880
the house.
举办儿童派对。

141
00:06:52.360 --> 00:06:54.420
That's what it's like to play Todd Packer.
这就是扮演托德·帕克的感觉。

142
00:06:56.500 --> 00:06:58.880
I could hear Kate Flannery's laugh.
我能听到凯特·弗兰纳里的笑声。

143
00:06:59.240 --> 00:07:01.000
Kate Flannery was on the stage with him.
凯特·弗兰纳里当时和他在同一个舞台上。

144
00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:01.220
Yeah.
是啊。

145
00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:01.700
Yeah.
对。

146
00:07:02.240 --> 00:07:07.040
So Angela, I think something we haven't talked about before is that there was an actor cast
所以安吉拉，我觉得我们以前没聊过的一点是，其实曾有一位演员被选中

147
00:07:07.040 --> 00:07:08.840
in the role of Todd Packer.
出演托德·帕克这个角色。

148
00:07:08.920 --> 00:07:09.080
Yeah.
是的。

149
00:07:09.380 --> 00:07:14.720
We shot for a couple days with him in the first season, and it just was not clicking.
我们在第一季和他一起拍了几天，但就是感觉不太对劲。

150
00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:15.380
Right.
没错。

151
00:07:15.680 --> 00:07:18.120
And they recast him with Dave Koechner.
然后他们换成了戴夫·科奇纳来演。

152
00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:20.040
And now he's got a whole episode.
现在他有一整集的戏了。

153
00:07:20.180 --> 00:07:21.080
Now he has a whole episode.
现在他拥有一整集了。

154
00:07:21.340 --> 00:07:25.360
And the minute, you know, to Dave's credit, the minute he walked on stage, he was Todd
而且一上台，你知道的，多亏了戴夫，他一走到台上，他就是托德

155
00:07:25.360 --> 00:07:25.740
Packer.
帕克。

156
00:07:25.860 --> 00:07:26.120
He was.
他确实是。

157
00:07:26.120 --> 00:07:26.900
We were like, oh my God.
我们当时就觉得，天哪。

158
00:07:27.020 --> 00:07:29.540
It's like you knew Rain would be Dwight, you know?
就像你知道雷恩会演德怀特一样，对吧？

159
00:07:29.740 --> 00:07:29.960
Yes.
没错。

160
00:07:30.100 --> 00:07:32.180
You knew Dave Koechner would be Todd Packer.
你知道戴夫·科奇纳就会是托德·帕克。

161
00:07:32.700 --> 00:07:38.880
Well, moving on to fast fact number three, I've got, you know, a little nerdy production
好吧，接下来是第三个冷知识，我这里有些，你知道的，比较书呆子气的制作专业

162
00:07:38.880 --> 00:07:40.400
speak coming your way.
术语要讲给你听。

163
00:07:40.680 --> 00:07:41.800
I know I love it.
我知道，我太喜欢了。

164
00:07:41.800 --> 00:07:42.340
I love it.
我喜欢。

165
00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:43.680
I love it when you geek out.
我喜欢你这种狂热的样子。

166
00:07:44.680 --> 00:07:48.980
Randy Cordray told me that this episode was a bottle show.
兰迪·科德雷告诉我这一集是一部“瓶装剧”。

167
00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:51.920
The name of this is called Bottle Show.
这一集的名称叫做瓶装剧。

168
00:07:52.060 --> 00:07:54.760
Look how tickled you are just saying bottled show.
看你光是说出“瓶装剧”这几个字就乐成什么样了。

169
00:07:55.100 --> 00:07:56.140
You're so tickled.
你太开心了。

170
00:07:56.520 --> 00:07:58.240
Tell us what a bottle show is.
给我们解释一下什么是瓶装剧。

171
00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:05.140
A bottle show is a Hollywood television term for an episode that basically stays within its
瓶装剧是好莱坞电视界的术语，指的是基本上只在既定的

172
00:08:05.140 --> 00:08:06.440
established sets.
场景中拍摄的一集。

173
00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:08.980
It doesn't have very many guest roles.
它没有太多的客串角色。

174
00:08:08.980 --> 00:08:14.860
It has very minimal stunts, minimal special effects, minimal visual effects.
它的特技极少，特效极少，视觉特效也极少。

175
00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:19.020
They are the least expensive episodes to produce in a season.
它们是一季中制作成本最低的剧集。

176
00:08:19.360 --> 00:08:23.220
Did we have to have so many bottle episodes a season for our budget?
为了我们的预算，我们一季是不是得拍好多集瓶装剧？

177
00:08:23.480 --> 00:08:24.700
Yes, Angela.
是的，安吉拉。

178
00:08:25.460 --> 00:08:31.940
Randy explained the budget process to me, which, again, I was geeking out.
兰迪向我解释了预算流程，对此，我再次化身狂热粉丝了。

179
00:08:32.300 --> 00:08:38.780
He said that the studio gave us a master budget each season, and it was a huge number.
他说制片厂每一季都会给我们一个总预算，那是一个巨大的数字。

180
00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:43.240
And he had to allocate it for the whole year for each episode.
他必须把这笔钱分配给整整一年的每一集。

181
00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:43.800
Yeah.
对。

182
00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:48.620
He would have to meet with our production accountant, who was named Carolyn Hayes.
他会跟我们的制作会计卡洛琳·海斯开会。

183
00:08:48.700 --> 00:08:49.720
I remember Carolyn.
我记得卡洛琳。

184
00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:50.460
Yes.
对的。

185
00:08:50.920 --> 00:08:56.560
And our UPM, Steve Burgess and Randy, they would all sit down together, and they would have to
还有我们的制片主任史蒂夫·伯吉斯和兰迪，他们会坐在一起，

186
00:08:56.560 --> 00:09:01.560
divide the budget into all the different categories that they had to pay for for a particular
把预算划分到特定一集所需支付的

187
00:09:01.560 --> 00:09:02.220
episode.
各个不同类别中。

188
00:09:02.440 --> 00:09:09.220
And that included salaries for all the cast and crew, writers, directors, rentals, editing,
这包括所有演员和剧组人员的薪水、编剧、导演、租金、剪辑、

189
00:09:09.460 --> 00:09:11.160
post-production, literally everything.
后期制作，简直涵盖了一切。

190
00:09:11.600 --> 00:09:13.460
Locations, props, music.
外景、道具、音乐。

191
00:09:13.700 --> 00:09:14.320
All of it.
全都有。

192
00:09:14.420 --> 00:09:16.120
That sounds so intimidating to me.
这听起来对我都太吓人了。

193
00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:21.400
That is like that, if a train left at 3 p.m., like, equation.
这就像是那种“如果一辆火车在下午3点出发”的数学题。

194
00:09:21.520 --> 00:09:23.060
No, please don't make me do that.
不，求求你别让我做那种事。

195
00:09:23.060 --> 00:09:28.900
So they would have a discussion with the writers to get sort of a general idea of what the season
所以他们会和编剧讨论，大致了解这一季会有什么

196
00:09:28.900 --> 00:09:35.540
was going to be like, but they had to set this budget not really knowing any scripts specifically.
样的走向，但他们在设定预算时，其实并不清楚任何具体的剧本。

197
00:09:35.540 --> 00:09:37.280
How do you do that?
这怎么做到？

198
00:09:37.600 --> 00:09:43.140
He said, you just do your best, and not all episodes end up costing the same.
他说，你只能尽力而为，而且并非所有剧集的最终成本都一样。

199
00:09:43.360 --> 00:09:46.780
Some of them went way over the per-episode budget.
其中有些剧集的开销远远超过了单集预算。

200
00:09:47.140 --> 00:09:51.960
Examples of those this season would be Threat Level Midnight, Andy's Play, and The Search.
这季当中的例子有《午夜威胁级别》、《安迪的戏剧》和《搜寻》.

201
00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:58.120
And in order to balance the books, the writers would have to include a certain number of bottle
为了平衡收支，编剧们不得不安排一定数量的室内剧

202
00:09:58.120 --> 00:09:58.560
shows.
集。

203
00:09:58.940 --> 00:10:00.940
And here's one of your bottle shows.
而这正是你们的一集室内剧。

204
00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:05.300
I feel like Carolyn and Randy and Steve Burgess would all be really good at that
我觉得卡罗琳、兰迪和史蒂夫·伯吉斯都会非常擅长那个

205
00:10:05.300 --> 00:10:08.340
Price is Right game where you have to guess the item's price.
《价格猜猜猜》节目，就是必须猜出商品价格的游戏。

206
00:10:09.260 --> 00:10:10.060
For sure.
绝对是的。

207
00:10:11.100 --> 00:10:12.700
Well, lady, that's all I got.
好了，女士，我只有这么多了。

208
00:10:12.980 --> 00:10:17.580
We could go to a break, and then when we come back, we have a very interesting cold open.
我们可以先休息一下，等回来后，我们会有一个非常有趣的片头前情提要。

209
00:10:17.820 --> 00:10:19.760
With the most disgusting sounds.
伴随着最令人作呕的声音。

210
00:10:20.100 --> 00:10:23.440
If you just listen to the cold open, it'll make you gag.
如果你只听这个片头，绝对会让你作呕。

211
00:10:23.840 --> 00:10:25.400
Oh, I didn't even think of that.
噢，我之前都没想到这一点。

212
00:10:25.720 --> 00:10:26.540
We'll be back.
我们马上回来。

213
00:10:26.800 --> 00:10:41.950
We are back, and that slurping noise you hear is Dwight having to eat all the canned foods
我们回来了，你听到的那种吸溜声是德怀特不得不吃掉所有

214
00:10:41.950 --> 00:10:44.190
that would have been in his bunker that might expire.
可能过期的、本该放在他避难所里的罐头食品。

215
00:10:44.450 --> 00:10:45.050
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

216
00:10:45.850 --> 00:10:46.970
It's so many things.
种类实在太多了。

217
00:10:47.090 --> 00:10:51.430
It's like canned tomatoes and canned mackerel and...
就像番茄罐头、鲭鱼罐头还有……

218
00:10:51.430 --> 00:10:55.970
Some kind of thing that looks like just really slimy okra.
某种看起来非常黏糊糊的秋葵一样的东西。

219
00:10:55.970 --> 00:10:57.010
I don't even know.
我甚至不知道那是什么。

220
00:10:57.230 --> 00:11:01.250
All of it is just slimy and in some kind of gelatinous liquid.
所有的东西都是黏糊糊的，还泡在某种胶状液体里。

221
00:11:01.670 --> 00:11:04.830
You know, I hoarded a bunch of food down in my basement.
你知道的，我在地下室囤了一堆食物。

222
00:11:05.330 --> 00:11:06.170
How'd that go?
结果怎么样？

223
00:11:07.030 --> 00:11:12.910
You know, it's kind of great because sometimes you go down there and you find a real treasure.
你知道的，其实挺棒的，因为有时你走下去会发现真正的宝贝。

224
00:11:12.910 --> 00:11:13.470
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

225
00:11:13.730 --> 00:11:19.270
But there was one night when I can't remember what happened, but the kids were off doing
但有天晚上，我记不清发生什么了，孩子们都在外面

226
00:11:19.270 --> 00:11:24.150
something and Lee was off doing something, and I didn't have time to go to the grocery
忙别的，李也在外面忙别的，而且我没时间去杂货

227
00:11:24.150 --> 00:11:24.430
store.
铺。

228
00:11:24.570 --> 00:11:26.850
And I thought, I'm just going to go to the basement and see what we got.
当时我想，我得去地下室看看我们有什么。

229
00:11:26.990 --> 00:11:27.330
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

230
00:11:27.330 --> 00:11:31.190
And all we had left was some expired pasta sauce.
结果我们只剩下一些过期的意面酱了。

231
00:11:31.670 --> 00:11:32.130
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

232
00:11:32.490 --> 00:11:33.690
But I was like...
但我当时觉得……

233
00:11:33.690 --> 00:11:34.870
How bad could it be?
能有多糟糕呢？

234
00:11:35.050 --> 00:11:35.390
Right?
对吧？

235
00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:41.210
So I made some pasta, and then I made the mistake of not tasting the pasta sauce firSt.
所以我煮了些意面，然后我犯了个错误，没有先尝尝意面酱的味道。

236
00:11:41.370 --> 00:11:41.630
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

237
00:11:41.630 --> 00:11:46.070
I doused my pasta, the last of the pasta, in the sauce.
我把酱汁倒在了我的意面上，那是家里仅剩的意面。

238
00:11:46.410 --> 00:11:47.390
It had turned.
它已经变质了。

239
00:11:47.690 --> 00:11:47.910
Yeah.
是啊。

240
00:11:48.230 --> 00:11:49.270
It was awful.
太可怕了。

241
00:11:49.630 --> 00:11:53.750
And I can't even remember what I had for dinner that night, but after that, I was kind
我甚至记不起那天晚上晚饭吃的什么了，但在那之后，我

242
00:11:53.750 --> 00:11:54.490
of like, done.
基本上就算了吧。

243
00:11:54.690 --> 00:11:58.470
So I do admire Dwight for keeping his eye on the expiration dates.
所以我确实很佩服德怀特能时刻留意保质期。

244
00:11:58.790 --> 00:12:00.070
Personal question for you.
问你个私人的问题。

245
00:12:00.210 --> 00:12:00.470
Yeah.
好啊。

246
00:12:00.990 --> 00:12:03.070
Would you be someone who would have a bunker?
你会是那种会建避难所的人吗？

247
00:12:03.350 --> 00:12:04.470
Why are you asking me that?
你为什么问我这个？

248
00:12:04.490 --> 00:12:04.970
Of course.
当然会。

249
00:12:05.130 --> 00:12:05.910
It's my dream.
那是我的梦想。

250
00:12:07.070 --> 00:12:07.470
It's...
那是...

251
00:12:07.470 --> 00:12:08.810
I daydream about it.
我做梦都在想。

252
00:12:09.470 --> 00:12:10.950
You daydream about your bunker.
你整天幻想着你的地堡。

253
00:12:11.150 --> 00:12:11.630
I love it.
我太喜欢了。

254
00:12:11.770 --> 00:12:14.010
Do you remember the bunker in the movie Grease 2?
你还记得电影《油脂2》里的那个地堡吗？

255
00:12:14.450 --> 00:12:14.850
No.
不记得。

256
00:12:14.970 --> 00:12:16.250
That they want to go make out in?
就是他们想去里面亲热的那个？

257
00:12:16.690 --> 00:12:19.250
Ever since I saw that movie in my youth, I've wanted one.
自从我年轻时看过那部电影，我就一直想要一个。

258
00:12:19.430 --> 00:12:21.530
I don't even know if I've ever seen Grease 2.
我甚至不知道自己有没有看过《油脂2》。

259
00:12:21.930 --> 00:12:22.330
What?
什么？

260
00:12:22.690 --> 00:12:23.290
Is that the Michelle Pfeiffer?
那是米歇尔·菲佛演的吗？

261
00:12:23.290 --> 00:12:24.630
I'm a smooth rider?
《我是个潇洒骑手》？

262
00:12:25.030 --> 00:12:26.010
Michelle Pfeiffer?
米歇尔·菲佛？

263
00:12:26.310 --> 00:12:28.070
I don't know if I've seen it all the way through.
我不知道自己有没有从头到尾看过。

264
00:12:28.490 --> 00:12:29.930
The bowling alley dance?
保龄球馆的那场舞？

265
00:12:29.930 --> 00:12:31.830
I don't even know what you're talking about.
我甚至不知道你在说什么。

266
00:12:32.090 --> 00:12:33.050
Oh, my God.
哦，天哪。

267
00:12:33.750 --> 00:12:35.330
What's the bowling alley dance?
什么是保龄球馆的舞？

268
00:12:35.330 --> 00:12:36.190
I can't.
我真是服了。

269
00:12:36.270 --> 00:12:38.050
I don't even know if I can keep talking to you right now.
我甚至不知道现在还能不能跟你聊下去。

270
00:12:40.590 --> 00:12:41.210
All right.
行吧。

271
00:12:41.430 --> 00:12:42.170
It's so good.
那太棒了。

272
00:12:42.550 --> 00:12:44.790
But yes, Angela, of course I want a bunker.
不过没错，安吉拉，我当然想要一个地堡。

273
00:12:45.150 --> 00:12:45.830
Have you met me?
你又不是不了解我？

274
00:12:45.930 --> 00:12:46.570
Do you want one?
你想要吗？

275
00:12:47.190 --> 00:12:49.750
I mean, if it would make you feel better.
我是说，如果这能让你感觉好受点的话。

276
00:12:50.690 --> 00:12:51.310
Here's the thing.
关键是这样的。

277
00:12:51.470 --> 00:12:53.150
I don't need everybody to have a bunker.
我并不是要求每个人都有地堡。

278
00:12:53.330 --> 00:12:54.070
I just want one.
我只是自己想要一个。

279
00:12:54.190 --> 00:12:55.110
Do you want one?
你想要吗？

280
00:12:55.250 --> 00:12:58.050
If the shit is really going to hit the fan that hard...
如果世界末日真的闹得那么大...

281
00:12:58.050 --> 00:12:58.230
Yeah.
对。

282
00:12:58.290 --> 00:13:00.150
...that you're going to go have to live in your bunker,
...大到你不得不去地堡里生活，

283
00:13:00.650 --> 00:13:02.890
what is the world you're coming out the door to?
等你推门出来面对的会是一个什么样的世界？

284
00:13:02.890 --> 00:13:04.650
I don't know, but I'm coming out.
我不知道，但我会出来的。

285
00:13:04.690 --> 00:13:05.650
I'm not sticking around for the zombies.
我可不会留下来跟僵尸纠缠。

286
00:13:05.870 --> 00:13:07.330
I'm coming out to see what it is.
我要出来看看外面到底成了什么样。

287
00:13:07.330 --> 00:13:08.570
I'm not sticking around for them.
我才不会留下来陪它们。

288
00:13:08.710 --> 00:13:10.690
When it all goes down, I'm going to be like,
当大难临头的时候，我会想，

289
00:13:10.790 --> 00:13:11.190
you know what?
你知道吗？

290
00:13:11.230 --> 00:13:13.990
I'm making margaritas, and I'm going to watch the fireworks.
我要做玛格丽塔酒，然后去看烟花。

291
00:13:14.470 --> 00:13:14.730
Hmm.
嗯。

292
00:13:15.050 --> 00:13:15.350
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

293
00:13:15.350 --> 00:13:20.090
It would be depressing to live in the bunker for like a month,
要在地堡里生活个一个月左右，然后你上来发现没有氧气，那得多沮丧啊。

294
00:13:20.090 --> 00:13:21.850
and then you come up, and there's no oxygen.
对啊。

295
00:13:22.170 --> 00:13:22.550
Yeah.
我是说，那可真是糟透了。

296
00:13:22.710 --> 00:13:24.010
I mean, that would really be shitty.
我只是这么一说。

297
00:13:24.610 --> 00:13:25.290
I'm just saying.
是啊。

298
00:13:25.630 --> 00:13:25.950
Yeah.
我可能还不如直接喝着玛格丽塔酒挺过去算了。

299
00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:28.150
I might just ride it out with some margaritas.
我懂你的意思。

300
00:13:28.350 --> 00:13:29.370
I hear you.
我明白。

301
00:13:30.050 --> 00:13:31.530
I also do want it.
我也确实想要这个。

302
00:13:32.250 --> 00:13:34.170
So I'm a little Dwight here.
所以我在这一段里有点像德怀特。

303
00:13:34.630 --> 00:13:37.770
As Dwight eats all of his slimy Slurpee food,
当德怀特吃着他那些黏糊糊的思乐冰食物时，

304
00:13:37.930 --> 00:13:39.950
he grosses everyone out, even Kevin.
他让所有人觉得恶心，连凯文都受不了。

305
00:13:40.490 --> 00:13:40.970
Yeah.
没错。

306
00:13:40.970 --> 00:13:42.730
They're like gagging.
他们都在作呕。

